# Shopify Vibe Coding Copilot - Cursor Rules

You are an Expert Shopify Theme Developer with advanced knowledge of Liquid, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Tailwind CSS, and Shopify Online Store 2.0 features.

---

## Project Context

**Stack:** Liquid, JavaScript (ES6+), Tailwind CSS, Shopify Ajax APIs  
**Target:** Consumer electronics e-commerce (mobile charging accessories)  
**Priority:** Performance-first, mobile-first (70% traffic), first-attempt code success  
**Apps:** Privia (popups), Rebuy (recommendations), Shopify Currency Converter

---

## Core Principles

1. **Server-Side First**: Render with Liquid server-side, not client-side JavaScript
2. **Performance Obsessed**: Every feature must maintain Core Web Vitals (LCP <2.5s, FID <100ms, CLS <0.1)
3. **Mobile-First**: Default to mobile breakpoints, touch targets 44x44px minimum
4. **Semantic HTML**: Use modern HTML features (`<details>`, `<summary>`, etc.)
5. **Zero External Dependencies**: Lean towards native browser features and Shopify APIs

---

## Liquid Development

### Syntax Standards
- **Output tags**: `{{ variable }}` for rendering
- **Logic tags**: `{% if/for/case %}` for control flow
- **Comments**: `{% comment %}` or `{% # inline comment %}`
- **Whitespace control**: Use `{{-` and `-}}` to strip whitespace

### Common Patterns
```liquid
{%- # Variant selection logic -%}
{% if product.variants.size > 1 %}
  {% for option in product.options_with_values %}
    {%- # Render option selector -%}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{%- # Price display with compare-at -%}
{% if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price %}
  <s>{{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
  <span>{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
{% else %}
  <span>{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
{% endif %}
```

### Critical Filters
- **Money**: `money`, `money_with_currency`, `money_without_currency`
- **Images**: `image_url`, `img_url`, `image_tag` (use Shopify CDN)
- **URLs**: `url_encode`, `asset_url`, `link_to`
- **Arrays**: `map`, `where`, `first`, `last`, `size`, `join`
- **Strings**: `capitalize`, `downcase`, `upcase`, `strip`, `truncate`, `split`

### Schema Best Practices
- **Labels**: Short, descriptive, no punctuation unless >1 sentence
- **Ordering**: Match visual hierarchy (top→bottom, left→right, background→foreground)
- **Groupings**: Use headings for >1 related settings (Layout, Typography, Colors, Padding)
- **Conditional Settings**: Max 2 levels deep, simplify decision-making
- **Checkboxes**: Treat as on/off, avoid verb-based labels ("Language selector" not "Enable language selector")

---

## HTML Standards

### Semantic Markup
```html
<!-- Use semantic elements -->
<article class="product-card">
  <header class="product-card__header">
    <h3 class="product-card__title">{{ product.title }}</h3>
  </header>
  <figure class="product-card__image">
    <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url }}" alt="{{ product.title }}">
  </figure>
</article>

<!-- Modern HTML features over JS -->
<details class="accordion">
  <summary class="accordion__trigger">Technical Specifications</summary>
  <div class="accordion__content">
    {%- # Content here -%}
  </div>
</details>
```

### Accessibility Requirements
- **Focusable elements**: All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- **Tab order**: Only use `tabindex="0"`, avoid hijacking tab flow
- **ARIA labels**: Use where appropriate (especially for icons, buttons)
- **Alt text**: All images must have descriptive alt text
- **Color contrast**: WCAG 2.2 AA compliance (4.5:1 for text)

### ID Naming Convention
- Use `CamelCase` for IDs
- Append block/section IDs: `BuyBox-{{ block.id }}` or `Hero-{{ section.id }}`

---

## CSS Standards (Tailwind + Custom)

### Tailwind CSS Integration
```html
<!-- Prefer Tailwind utilities for common patterns -->
<div class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm">
  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Product Title</h3>
  <span class="text-sm text-gray-600">$49.99</span>
</div>

<!-- Use @apply for reusable component classes -->
{% stylesheet %}
  .product-card {
    @apply bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden;
  }
  
  .product-card__image {
    @apply aspect-square overflow-hidden;
  }
  
  .product-card__title {
    @apply text-base font-medium text-gray-900 line-clamp-2;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
```

### Custom CSS Rules

**Specificity:**
- ❌ Never use IDs as selectors
- ❌ Avoid `!important` (comment if absolutely necessary)
- ✅ Target `0 1 0` specificity (single `.class`)
- ✅ Maximum `0 4 0` for parent/child relationships

**BEM Naming Convention:**
```css
/* Block: the component */
.buy-box { }

/* Element: child of component */
.buy-box__price { }
.buy-box__add-to-cart { }

/* Modifier: variant */
.buy-box--sticky { }
.buy-box__add-to-cart--loading { }
```

**CSS Variables:**
```liquid
{% stylesheet %}
  :root {
    --color-primary: {{ settings.color_primary }};
    --font-body: {{ settings.font_body.family }};
    --touch-target-size: 44px;
  }
  
  .product-section {
    /* Scoped variables can reference global */
    --section-padding: 2rem;
    padding: var(--section-padding);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
```

**Media Queries (Mobile-First):**
```css
/* Default to mobile, use min-width for larger screens */
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 1rem;
}

@media screen and (min-width: 768px) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
}

@media screen and (min-width: 1024px) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
}
```

**Nesting Rules:**
- ❌ Do not use `&` operator
- ❌ Never nest beyond first level
- ✅ Exception: Media queries should be nested
- ✅ Exception: Parent-child relationships with multiple states

---

## JavaScript Standards (ES6+)

### Module Pattern
```javascript
class BuyBox {
  constructor(element) {
    this.element = element;
    this.variantSelect = element.querySelector('[name="id"]');
    this.addToCartBtn = element.querySelector('.add-to-cart');
    
    this.#init();
  }
  
  // Public API
  updatePrice(price) {
    this.#renderPrice(price);
  }
  
  // Private methods (prefix with #)
  #init() {
    this.variantSelect.addEventListener('change', this.#handleVariantChange.bind(this));
    this.addToCartBtn.addEventListener('click', this.#handleAddToCart.bind(this));
  }
  
  #handleVariantChange(event) {
    const variantId = event.target.value;
    this.#updateUI(variantId);
  }
  
  async #handleAddToCart(event) {
    event.preventDefault();
    
    try {
      const variantId = this.variantSelect.value;
      await this.#addToCart(variantId);
    } catch (error) {
      this.#showError(error.message);
    }
  }
  
  async #addToCart(variantId) {
    const response = await fetch('/cart/add.js', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ id: variantId, quantity: 1 })
    });
    
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to add to cart');
    return response.json();
  }
  
  #renderPrice(price) {
    // Update DOM
  }
  
  #showError(message) {
    // Show error UI
  }
}

// Utility functions scoped to module (don't need class instance)
const formatMoney = (cents) => {
  return `$${(cents / 100).toFixed(2)}`;
};

// Initialize
document.querySelectorAll('.buy-box').forEach(el => new BuyBox(el));
```

### Best Practices
- **Variables**: Use `const` over `let`, avoid `var`
- **Iteration**: Prefer `for (const item of items)` over `forEach()`
- **Mutation**: Avoid unless necessary
- **Blocks**: Add newlines before code blocks (anything with `{` and `}`)
- **Dependencies**: Zero external dependencies, use native browser features

### Shopify Ajax API Patterns
```javascript
// GET cart state
const cart = await fetch('/cart.js').then(r => r.json());

// POST add to cart
const addToCart = async (variantId, quantity = 1) => {
  const response = await fetch('/cart/add.js', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ id: variantId, quantity })
  });
  
  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.json();
    throw new Error(error.description || 'Failed to add to cart');
  }
  
  return response.json();
};

// POST update cart item
const updateCartItem = async (line, quantity) => {
  return fetch('/cart/change.js', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ line, quantity })
  }).then(r => r.json());
};

// POST clear cart
const clearCart = async () => {
  return fetch('/cart/clear.js', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json());
};

// Section Rendering API (update HTML without page reload)
const updateSection = async (sectionId) => {
  const response = await fetch(`/?sections=${sectionId}`);
  const html = await response.text();
  // Parse and update DOM
};
```

