## Critical Reminders

### Before Generating Code
1. ✅ Check if native HTML/CSS can solve it (avoid unnecessary JS)
2. ✅ Consider performance impact (will this slow down LCP/CLS?)
3. ✅ Mobile-first approach (70% of traffic)
4. ✅ Accessibility compliance (keyboard navigation, screen readers)
5. ✅ Integration with existing apps (Privia, Rebuy, Currency Converter)

### Code Quality Checklist
- [ ] Server-side rendered with Liquid where possible
- [ ] Images optimized (Shopify CDN, lazy loading, srcset)
- [ ] JavaScript deferred or async loaded
- [ ] CSS scoped to components, BEM naming
- [ ] Touch targets ≥44x44px for mobile
- [ ] Semantic HTML elements used
- [ ] No hardcoded values (use CSS variables)
- [ ] Commented complex logic
- [ ] Tested on mobile viewport

### Common Pitfalls to Avoid
- ❌ Client-side rendering what could be server-side
- ❌ Loading all JS on all pages (conditional loading!)
- ❌ Inline styles (use CSS variables)
- ❌ Large unoptimized images
- ❌ Complex CSS selectors (keep specificity low)
- ❌ Missing alt text on images
- ❌ Forgetting mobile breakpoints

---

## Testing & Validation

### Performance Testing
- Google Lighthouse (target: Performance 90+, Accessibility 100)
- Core Web Vitals (LCP <2.5s, FID <100ms, CLS <0.1)
- Mobile performance (test on throttled 3G)

### Browser Testing
- Chrome, Firefox, Safari (desktop + mobile)
- iOS Safari (primary mobile browser)
- Test on real devices when possible

### Shopify Theme Check
```bash
shopify theme check
```

---

**Remember:** Every line of code should prioritize performance, accessibility, and mobile-first design. When in doubt, choose the simpler solution that works server-side with Liquid over complex client-side JavaScript.
